# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One rule: any folder whose name ends in _data is yours alone.
#
# Git ignores everything inside it and tracks only its README.md. Survey
# exports, ad platform pulls, licensed research, and customer records stay on
# your machine. A public repository keeps history even after you delete a
# file, so the safe default is enforced here rather than left to discipline.
#
# To track something inside a _data folder anyway: git add -f <path>
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

**/*_data/**
!**/*_data/README.md

# The working area. Outputs are disposable by design.
99_Outputs/**
!99_Outputs/README.md

# Common data formats, anywhere in the tree, as a second line of defense
*.csv
*.tsv
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.zip
*.pdf
*.sqlite
*.db

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
credentials.*
secrets.*

# OS and editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log
